{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-hopf-diquark","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:hopf-diquark","kind":"definition","title":"Hopf diquark","tags":["diquark","hopf","cooper-pair","color-superconductivity","color-antitriplet"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.Archimedean.HopfDiquark","text":"hopf-diquark.md","leanSource":"hopf-diquark.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:hopf-diquark\"></a><p>A <strong>Hopf diquark</strong> is a pair of quarks <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\mathfrak{q}_i^a, \\mathfrak{q}_j^b)</code> in distinct color tubes <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">a \\neq b</code> of Bring's surface, joined by the Hopf link <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{L}_H</code>:</p>\n<pre><code class=\"language-math math-display\">  D_{ij}^{[ab]}\n  = \n  \\mathfrak{q}_i^a  \\oplus  \\mathfrak{q}_j^b,</code></pre>\n<p>where <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">i, j \\in \\{\\mathfrak{u}, \\mathfrak{d}, \\mathfrak{s}\\}</code> denote flavor indices and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">a, b \\in \\{r, g, b\\}</code> denote color indices. The bracket <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">[ab]</code> denotes antisymmetry: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">D_{ij}^{[ab]} = -D_{ij}^{[ba]}</code>.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/hopf-diquark.md","heading":"Definition","number":"17.15.5","page":"b/def-hopf-diquark","qa":{"counts":{"pass":76,"fail":0,"warn":2,"na":14,"unknown":0,"stale":79},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:QOU.MassTheory.Archimedean.HopfDiquark","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/observations/hopf-diquark.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
